[21.000859, "o", "child processes for TCP requests: in use %zu, highest since last SIGUSR1 %zu, max allowed %zu.\r\nserver %s#%d: queries sent %u, retried %u, failed %u, nxdomain replies %u, avg. latency %ums\r\nHost                           Address                                  Flags      Expires                  Source\r\nNXNAME\r\nIXFR\r\nAXFR\r\nDNSSEC signature expired\r\nstale NXDOMAIN\r\nsignature expired before valid\r\n<TXT>\r\n<MX>\r\n%.2x%s\r\n"]
[21.001203, "o", "951yZDNLERKzowefnbvhdkqr:m:p:c:l:s:i:t:u:g:a:x:S:C:A:T:H:Q:I:B:F:G:O:M:X:V:U:j:P:J:W:Y:2:4:6:7:8:0:3:\r\nPXEClient\r\nmust have exactly one resolv.conf to read domain from.\r\nsyntax check OK\r\ncannot execute %s: %s\r\nerror executing %s: %s\r\nextraneous parameter\r\nmx-host\r\nmx-target\r\ndomain-suffix\r\nbogus-nxdomain\r\nselfmx\r\nexpand-hosts\r\nlocalmx\r\nno-\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K20-encode\r\ndo-\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K20-encode\r\nexcept-interface\r\ndhcp-lease-max\r\nedns-packet-max\r\ntxt-record\r\ndns-forward-max\r\ntftp-max\r\ndhcp-pxe-vendor\r\nmax-ttl\r\nmax-cache-ttl\r\nmax-port\r\npxe-prompt\r\npxe-service\r\ndhcp-proxy\r\nproxy-dnssec\r\nmax-tcp-connections\r\nTreat ipaddr as NXDOMAIN (defeats Verisign wildcard).\r\nReturn self-pointing MX records for local hosts.\r\nExpand simple names in /etc/hosts with domain-suffix.\r\ntag-expression\r\nEvaluate conditional tag expression.\r\nSpecify vendor class to match for PXE requests.\r\nReturn MX records for local hosts.\r\nSpecify an MX record.\r\n[=<max_expired>]\r\nUse expired cache data for faster reply.\r\nDHCP option sent only to PXE clients.\r\nMaximum supported UDP packet size for EDNS.0 (defaults to %s).\r\nSet maximum number of random originating ports for a query.\r\n<addr>/<prefix>,<ipaddr>\r\nSpecify default target in an MX record.\r\nSpecify time-to-live in seconds for maximum TTL to send to clients.\r\nSpecify maximum number of DHCP leases (defaults to %s).\r\n<name>,<txt>[,<txt]\r\nSpecify TXT DNS record.\r\nSpecify extra networks sharing a broadcast domain for DHCP\r\nExecute file and read configuration from stdin.\r\nMaximum number of concurrent DNS queries. (defaults to %s)\r\nDo NOT reuse filename and server fields for extra DHCP options.\r\nExport files by TFTP only from the specified subtree.\r\nMaximum number of concurrent TFTP transfers (defaults to %s).\r\nMaximum MTU to use for TFTP transfers.\r\nDisable the TFTP blocksize extension.\r\nExtra logging for DHCP.\r\nUse these DHCP relays as full proxies.\r\nPrompt to send to PXE clients.\r\nBoot service for PXE menu.\r\nCheck configuration syntax.\r\n[=base64|text]\r\n<text>\r\nProxy DNSSEC validation results from upstream nameservers.\r\nExport local names to global DNS\r\nDomain to export to global DNS\r\n<domain>,<range>,[<prefix>]\r\n<hex>\r\nCall dhcp-script when lease expiry changes.\r\nSuppress DNS bit \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K20 encoding.\r\nEnable DNS bit \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K20 encoding.\r\nDo not add CHAOS TXT records.\r\nMaximum number of concurrent tcp connections.\r\nbad MX preference\r\nbad MX name\r\nbad MX target\r\nexclude:\r\nbad prefix length\r\nbad prefix\r\nprefix length too small\r\ntext\r\nextra\r\nprefix length must be exactly 64 for RA subnets\r\nprefix length must be exactly 64 for subnet constructors\r\nprefix length must be at least 64\r\nprefix must be zero with \"constructor:\" argument\r\nbad hex constant\r\nbad IPv6 prefix\r\nx86PC\r\nArc_x86\r\nx86-64_EFI\r\nXscale_EFI\r\nbad dhcp-proxy address\r\nbad TXT record\r\nbad IPv4 prefix length\r\nbad IPv6 prefix length\r\n%.1x.\r\nNo vendor-encap options allowed in dhcp-option-pxe\r\nMaximum number of concurrent DNS queries reached (max: %d)\r\nMaximum number of concurrent DNS queries to %s reached (max: %d)\r\nCase mismatch in DNS reply - check bit \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K20 encoding.\r\ntry increasing /proc/sys/net/core/optmem_max\r\nmax_port cannot be smaller than min_port\r\nwarning: interface %s does not currently exist\r\nDHCP, sockets bound exclusively to interface %s\r\nrestricting maximum simultaneous TFTP transfers to %d\r\nTCP helper process %u died unexpectedly\r\nscript process exited with status %d\r\nfailed to execute %s: %s\r\nexiting on receipt of SIGTERM\r\nlease-init script returned exit code %s\r\n%.2x-\r\n%.2x\r\n%.2x:\r\n%.2x\r\nPXE BIS not supported\r\nproxy-ignored\r\n%u next server: %s\r\nPXE menu too large\r\nDNSMASQ_LEASE_EXPIRES\r\n%.2x-%.2x-%.2x-%.2x-%.2x-%.2x/\r\n, prefix deprecated\r\n%s, proxy on subnet %.0s%s%.0s%.0s\r\nextension-path\r\nmax-datagram-reassembly\r\nx-windows-fs\r\nx-windows-dm\r\nmax-message-size\r\nposix-timezone\r\nRTR-ADVERT(%s) %s old prefix\r\n<AXFR>\r\n%s%02x%02x\r\npool memory in use %zu, max %zu, allocated %zu\r\n%.8x\r\nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/\r\n%u dumping packet %u mask \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K0x\u001b[m\u001b[K%04x\r\ndnssec"]
